---
title: Miso Sweet Potato and Broccoli Bowl
description: Roasted sweet potatoes and broccoli over rice, with a miso-sesame dressing and toasted sesame seeds.
tags: [sheet-pan, fall]
course: main
icons: [bowl-rice, broccoli, potato]
source:
  name: Smitten Kitchen
  author: Deb Perelman
  url: https://smittenkitchen.com/2013/10/miso-sweet-potato-and-broccoli-bowl/
servings: 4
time: 50m
---

Heat the oven to 400°F (200°C). Cook the @rice{1%cup}(dry, or another grain) in a #rice cooker{} or on the stove, following the package directions.

Peel the @sweet potatoes{1 1/2%lb}(1 to 2) and cut them into 1-inch cubes. Cut the @broccoli{1%lb}(1 large bundle) into bite-sized florets. Peel the stems if they're woody, then cut them into 1/2- to 1-inch pieces.

Coat a large #sheet pan{} (or two smaller ones) with a thin layer of @olive oil{1-2%tbsp}. Spread the sweet potatoes on the pan and season with @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{}(freshly ground). Roast for ~roast{20%minutes}, until browned underneath.

Flip the sweet potatoes and add the broccoli. Season again with salt and pepper, and roast for another ~roast{10-20%minutes}, until the broccoli is lightly charred at the edges and the sweet potatoes are deeply browned and tender. Toss once more if they're cooking unevenly.

While the vegetables roast, toast the @white sesame seeds{1%tsp} and @black sesame seeds{1%tsp} in a #small skillet{} until fragrant, then let them cool.

Make the dressing: In a #blender{}, combine the @fresh ginger{1%tbsp}(minced), @garlic clove{1}(small, minced), @white miso{2%tbsp}(the mildest kind), @tahini{2%tbsp}(or another nut butter in a pinch), @honey{1%tbsp}(or agave nectar, to keep it vegan), @rice vinegar{1/4%cup}, @toasted sesame oil{2%tbsp}, and @&olive oil{2%tbsp}. Blend until smooth, scraping down the sides once. Taste and adjust, but don't add honey to fix saltiness. The sweet potatoes want that salt.

Scoop the rice into bowls and pile on the sweet potatoes and broccoli. Drizzle lightly with the dressing and finish with the sesame seeds. Serve with extra dressing on the side.
